      },
      "message": "fix(recognize): read a slot with holes through or tangent to its floor\n\ndetect_pockets returned nothing for the p01-flange slot. Two through\nholes in its floor are tangent to the slot wall, so the floor's rings\nshare a vertex, and the feature walk reported every ring as open. With\nthe holes off the wall, any inner ring still refused the slot.\n\n- slot_of refuses a boss only: an inner ring whose edge facets stand\n  above the floor. A hole through the floor keeps the slot.\n- recognize::pinch takes the walk's knotted rings as the outer ring and\n  its holes only when it proves them: simple rings of face boundary\n  edges, holes inside the largest ring, and the area identity with the\n  face's facet area. Anything else stays refused.\n\nPinned by a_slot_with_a_hole_tangent_to_its_wall_is_still_a_slot,\na_slot_with_holes_through_its_floor_is_still_a_slot and\na_boss_standing_in_the_channel_is_not_a_slot (mcp_pockets).\n\nFixes #2440\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
